# Every path requires review from the owner before merge.
# The ruleset "protect-main" enforces code-owner review on the default branch.
# @sevn-one is a second code owner (a user account). GitHub Apps cannot be named
# in CODEOWNERS, so an App review cannot satisfy code-owner review.
#
# Dependabot pull requests are the one exception to a human review:
# .github/workflows/dependabot-approve.yml approves them with a code-owner
# user account's token, and only when a PR's net diff is exactly Dependabot's
# own signed commit. See .github/CONTRIBUTING.md, "Dependabot code-owner
# approval".
#
# Both owners MUST stay on one line: CODEOWNERS resolves each file to only
# its LAST matching pattern, so two separate `*` lines (as briefly landed
# directly on main in 9ddd546) silently drop every owner but the last one —
# `* @sevn-one` alone, with @alexhawat dropped as a code owner entirely.
